  "id": "fixed-interval-schedule",
  "term": "fixed-interval schedule",
  "definition": "A fixed-interval schedule is a learning arrangement in which reward delivery depends on a set amount of time passing before reinforcement is available. It is used to study temporal control, or how behavior is guided by timing.",
